                                "sense_id": "61bc05b0-60ec-3854-a829-f09bf306e655",
                                "text": "About the middle of the sixteenth century, Darren, and the adjoining mine of Cwm Symlog, were extensively and profitably worked […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ac77cb7f-6f56-46bc-9979-57e8d63c70ad",
                                "sense_id": "61bc05b0-60ec-3854-a829-f09bf306e655",
                                "text": "[…] the sun shone down merrily on the green woods of Darren, the bright Liffey tumbled joyously down by bank and brake, and a joyous peal of bells rang out to welcome the happy bridal of the Lady of Darren and her handsome lover, Sir Brian Courtenay."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
